  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The classification system and empirical findings are restricted to the area within Beijing's 5th Ring Road and may not directly generalize to other metropolitan contexts.",
      "what": "Using clustering algorithms on multi-source geographical big data, this study delineated 67 commercial districts within Beijing's 5th Ring Road. The districts were evaluated across four dimensions—scale and composition, vitality and temporal heterogeneity, radiation, and location and environment—and categorized into seven distinct operational patterns, such as City-level Core, Suburban Hub, and Weekday-oriented Local.",
      "why": "It replaces simplified classification schemes with a multi-dimensional, data-driven taxonomy that captures how commercial districts actually function across different times of the week, enabling planners to tailor revitalization strategies to specific district profiles."
    }
